[BLAME] benchmark_1/parts/semver_solver/lib/semver_solver_impl.py: The GT comparator evaluation branch at line 377 remains unexcluded dead code under low/semver_solver.pyi: range compilation never constructs a GT comparator, because greater-than comparators are normalized to the immediately higher boundary and evaluated with GE (likewise '<=' and hyphen upper bounds use LE/LT), so no conforming range expression can ever route a GT comparator into comparator evaluation. The branch at line 377 is therefore structurally unreachable and must be pruned together with its unused GT alias, or excluded by placing '# pragma: no cover (assumption: > normalizes to a GE boundary)' on the statement itself.
[BLAME] benchmark_1/parts/semver_solver/lib/semver_solver_impl.py: The unreachable fallback return at line 280 is still counted by the coverage oracle: the '# pragma: no cover (assumption: operator is restricted by the range clause grammar)' annotation was placed on the standalone comment line preceding the statement, which does not exclude the following return, so the statement at line 280 remains reported as uncovered. No conforming range expression can reach this fallback, so either move the exclusion annotation onto the return statement line itself or restructure the expansion so the fallback statement is eliminated while preserving the declared return type.
[BLAME] benchmark_1/parts/semver_solver/tests/semver_solver_impl_test.py: The malformed-syntax precondition of parse_range remains incompletely exercised: the postcondition set covers full semantic versions carrying build metadata, but no test exercises rejection of range text whose version token carries a '+' separator with no build identifiers (for example a trailing '+') or otherwise contains an empty or non-alphanumeric-hyphen build identifier. Such tokens violate Semantic Versioning 2.0.0 grammar and therefore the range grammar, so the malformed-syntax precondition requires them to raise InvalidRangeError, just as the already covered empty pre-release and invalid identifier rejections do.
[CHANGE] benchmark_1/parts/semver_solver/tests/semver_solver_impl_test.py: Address build-metadata grammar feedback: extend parse_range malformed-syntax rejection to cover version tokens with a trailing '+' separator and no build identifiers (>=1.0.0+, and hyphen bound 1.0.0 - 2.0.0+), empty build identifiers (>=1.0.0+build..1), and build identifiers with non-alphanumeric-hyphen characters (>=1.0.0+build_1), all asserting InvalidRangeError with raw_range preserved.
[CHANGE] benchmark_1/parts/semver_solver/lib/semver_solver_impl.py: Address feedback (2 items): (1) pruned the structurally unreachable GT comparator evaluation branch in _evaluate_comparator together with the unused GT alias (and the equally unused LE alias) in _expand_operator, since greater-than comparators normalize to the next GE boundary during range compilation and hyphen-range full upper bounds are the sole LE producer, leaving GE as the final fallthrough with a comment documenting the normalization; (2) moved the exclusion annotation onto the return statement line itself: 'return []  # pragma: no cover (assumption: operator is restricted by the range clause grammar)', so the fallback is properly excluded while preserving the declared non-Optional return type
